    In this study, we evaluate our method against a baseline DRL approach, an analytical

     solution under the same communication environment, and a teacher-student framework.

     Experimental results demonstrate that our method outperforms both the mathematical
     solution and teacher-student models under the same conditions, validating the superior-
     ity of our approach.

   The rest of the thesis is organized as follows. Chapter 2 describes related work and mo-

tivation. Chapter 3 introduces the system model, problem formulation, basic concepts, and
comparison of Catfish-DRL with adversarial models. Chapter 4 describes the CDRL scheme.
Chapter 5 shows the simulation results. Finally, chapter 6 concludes the thesis.




