4.2.2 Catfish agent of of Catfish-effect-based DRL

       This phase continues the work from phase 4.2.1 by explaining the dedicated mechanisms
of the catfish agent and how it collaborates with the main agent. The goal is to achieve both

the stimulation of exploration by the main agent and experience-level knowledge transfer. The
core design of the catfish agent includes three key aspects, all aimed at ensuring its policy
outperforms that of the main agent: first, during the data pre-generation phase in phase 4.1,

all experiences are routed based on an energy efficiency (EE) threshold. Second, the discount
factor of the catfish agent is set higher to emphasize long-term return estimation. Third,
an adaptive competitive reward mechanism is established to encourage the catfish agent to

maintain its leading advantage.

