B. Catfish Strategy 2: Asymmetric Discounting Strategy

    The discount factor is a critical hyperparameter in reinforcement learning that deter-

mines an RL agent’s emphasis on future rewards. This hyperparameter influences the agent’s
policy, convergence speed, and long-term optimization capability. In A. Catfish Strategy 1:
Experience Stratification, this thesis describes why experiences are stratified. Our purpose in

adjusting the discount factor is to extend the idea of assigning different tasks to different tiers,
configuring the discount factors of the main agent and the catfish agent according to their
respective tasks. This approach helps avoid strategy homogenization, thereby encouraging

                                                    34
differentiated strategies between agents. As a result, the main agent focuses on short-term
demands to accelerate convergence, while the catfish agent emphasizes long-term objectives

to pursue optimal outcomes.


